## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end multi-tenant design, runtime feature toggles, schema evolution, and deterministic replay using AWS DVA primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation with Lake Formation and tenant-scoped keys
- Schema evolution via Glue Schema Registry with backward/forward compatibility
- Deterministic replay using per-tenant replay token in DynamoDB
- Idempotent writes by deduping event_id in DynamoDB
- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry; secure access controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dedupe and write path
async function processEvent(evt){
  const {tenant_id, event_id, payload} = evt;
  // ensure idempotent dedupe
  const exists = await dynamo.get({TableName:'TenantDedup', Key:{tenant_id, event_id}});
  if (exists.Item) return;
  await dynamo.put({TableName:'TenantDedup', Item:{tenant_id, event_id, ts: Date.now()}});
  // write raw to S3 with partition tenant/date (implementation omitted)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle a schema-breaking change in a live tenant dataset?
- How would you validate replay correctness under a backfill window?

## Why This Is Asked
